IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nlca-dates`
IMPORT `nlca-rules`
IMPORT `nlca-seat`

-- Limitation Act 1981 (NT), child abuse provisions -- worked cases for the survivor's questions (nlca-seat.l4) and the
-- date helpers (nlca-dates.l4, nlca-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law.
-- The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the day`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `Dates`

-- The 18th birthday: the same day 18 years on; from 29 February, 28 February (F2).
#ASSERT `the 18th birthday of a person born on` (`d` 10 3 2000) EQUALS `d` 10 3 2018
#ASSERT `the 18th birthday of a person born on` (`d` 29 2 2000) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2018
#ASSERT `the 18th birthday of a person born on` (`d` 31 12 1999) EQUALS `d` 31 12 2017
-- "before the commencement": 14 June 2017 is, 15 June 2017 is not (F3).
#ASSERT (`d` 14 6 2017) `is before the 2017 commencement`
#ASSERT (NOT ((`d` 15 6 2017) `is before the 2017 commencement`))
#ASSERT (NOT ((`d` 16 6 2017) `is before the 2017 commencement`))

§§ `s 5A(6) -- was it child abuse`

-- Born 10 March 2000: under 18 to the end of 9 March 2018.
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 9 3 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 10 3 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `serious physical abuse` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `serious physical abuse` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 1 1 2019) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Psychological abuse counts only where it arises from sexual or serious physical abuse (para (c)).
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `psychological abuse` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `psychological abuse` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 1 1 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `psychological abuse` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 10 3 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Other harm is not in the list, however young the person was.
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `other harm or ill-treatment` FALSE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 1 1 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `other harm or ill-treatment` TRUE (`d` 10 3 2000) (`d` 1 1 2005) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Born 29 February 2000: turns 18 on 28 February 2018 (F2).
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`d` 29 2 2000) (`d` 27 2 2018) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`d` 29 2 2000) (`d` 28 2 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Abuse long before the Act (1975): s 5A(6) has no date limit ("is (or was) under 18").
#ASSERT `Was what was done to me child abuse` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`d` 1 7 1965) (`d` 1 7 1975) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 5, 5A -- the time limit`

-- A survivor born 1 January 1980, sexually abused on 1 June 1990 (age 10).
GIVEN `the action` IS A `Kind of action`, `arose` IS A BOOLEAN, `other Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect of section 5A`
`abused at 10` `the action` `arose` `other Act` MEANS
    `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `sexual abuse` FALSE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 6 1990) `the action` `arose` `other Act`

`own` MEANS `my own action for damages for personal injury`
`FIA` MEANS `a family action under the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 for the death of the person abused`
`estate` MEANS `an action for the estate of the person abused, on a cause of action that survived the death`
`not PI` MEANS `an action that is not for damages for personal injury`
`no limit` MEANS `no limitation period under this Act: the action may be brought at any time`
`not decided` MEANS `not decided by section 5A: the action is not one for damages for personal injury from child abuse`
`not abuse` MEANS `section 5A does not apply: it was not child abuse as s 5A(6) defines it`
`other Act applies` MEANS `another Act's limitation period applies: this Act does not apply (s 5)`

-- s 5A(2): no limitation period for my own action; s 5A(4)(a), (b): nor for the family's death claim or the estate's.
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `own` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `FIA` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `estate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
-- Outside s 5A(1)'s own wording: not for damages for personal injury, or the injury did not arise from the abuse.
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `not PI` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not decided`
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `own` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not decided`
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `FIA` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not decided`
-- s 5: another Act's period still applies (finding 2).
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `own` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `other Act applies`
#ASSERT `abused at 10` `estate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `other Act applies`
-- Not child abuse: the day of the 18th birthday (1 January 1998) and the day before.
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `serious physical abuse` FALSE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 31 12 1997) `own` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `serious physical abuse` FALSE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 1 1998) `own` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not abuse`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `other harm or ill-treatment` FALSE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 6 1990) `own` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not abuse`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `other harm or ill-treatment` FALSE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 6 1990) `own` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not abuse`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `psychological abuse` TRUE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 6 1990) `own` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no limit`
#ASSERT `Is there a time limit on my child abuse action` `psychological abuse` FALSE (`d` 1 1 1980) (`d` 1 6 1990) `own` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not abuse`

§§ `s 5A(5) -- the court's other powers`

#ASSERT `Can the court still dismiss or stay my action for delay` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court still dismiss or stay my action for delay` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the court still dismiss or stay my action for delay` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the court still dismiss or stay my action for delay` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 53-55 -- an earlier case`

`none` MEANS `there was no earlier case`
`limitation judgment` MEANS `a judgment that the limitation period had expired`
`LPN judgment` MEANS `a judgment on legal professional negligence given on the ground that the limitation period had expired`
`other grounds` MEANS `a judgment finally deciding the matter on other grounds`
`settled out of time` MEANS `a settlement agreement made because the claim was out of time`
`settled otherwise` MEANS `a settlement agreement made for other reasons`
`pending` MEANS `an action brought that had no judgment by 15 June 2017`

`may sue` MEANS `I may sue despite the earlier judgment, as if the earlier action had not been commenced`
`directly` MEANS `section 5A applies directly: no limitation period under this Act`
`pending removed` MEANS `section 5A removes the limitation period from my pending action`
`cannot` MEANS `I cannot sue again: a court finally decided the matter on other grounds before 15 June 2017`
`unclear` MEANS `the Act does not clearly say`
`after 2017` MEANS `Part V Division 2 does not reach a judgment or settlement made on or after 15 June 2017`
`other period` MEANS `Part V Division 2 does not reach it: the period was not one fixed by this Act or an Act it repealed`

-- Not a child abuse action: the Division is read as not reaching it (F5).
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` FALSE `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 3 2005) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `not a child abuse action: Part V Division 2 is not read as reaching it`
-- No earlier case: s 5A alone.
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `none` `any day` `any day` TRUE EQUALS `directly`
-- s 54(1), (4): a limitation judgment on 14 June 2017 (the last day before the commencement) and on 15 June 2017.
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `limitation judgment` (`d` 14 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `may sue`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `limitation judgment` (`d` 15 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `after 2017`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 3 2005) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `may sue`
-- s 53(1): a judgment on another Act's period is not on a "limitation period" of the Division.
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 3 2005) `any day` FALSE EQUALS `other period`
-- s 54(2): legal professional negligence.
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `LPN judgment` (`d` 1 3 2005) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `may sue`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `LPN judgment` (`d` 20 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `after 2017`
-- s 54(3): a final judgment on other grounds bars a new action, whatever period applied; not one after 15 June 2017.
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `other grounds` (`d` 14 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `cannot`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `other grounds` (`d` 14 6 2017) `any day` FALSE EQUALS `cannot`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `other grounds` (`d` 15 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `after 2017`
-- s 53(2): settlements (F4).
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `settled out of time` (`d` 1 1 2010) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `may sue`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `settled out of time` (`d` 15 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `after 2017`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `settled otherwise` (`d` 1 1 2010) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `unclear`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `settled otherwise` (`d` 20 6 2017) `any day` TRUE EQUALS `after 2017`
-- s 55: brought on 14 June 2017 with no judgment by 15 June 2017; brought on 15 June 2017 (s 5A directly).
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `pending` `any day` (`d` 14 6 2017) TRUE EQUALS `pending removed`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `pending` `any day` (`d` 15 6 2017) TRUE EQUALS `directly`
#ASSERT `Can I sue now after my earlier case` TRUE `pending` `any day` (`d` 1 1 2016) FALSE EQUALS `other period`

§§ `s 54(5)(a), (6), (7) -- setting aside`

`SC hearing` MEANS `the Supreme Court, hearing my new action`
`SC application` MEANS `the Supreme Court, on an application, not hearing my new action`
`other hearing` MEANS `another court, hearing my new action`
`other not hearing` MEANS `another court, not hearing my new action`

#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC hearing` `a different court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 54(6): the Supreme Court on application, not hearing the action.
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC application` `a different court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `settled out of time` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC application` `no court: it was a settlement agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if it considers it is just and reasonable".
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC hearing` `the same court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `other hearing` `a different court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 54(7): another court, its own judgment yes, another court's no; a settlement is no court's judgment (F6).
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `other hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `LPN judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `other hearing` `a different court` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `settled out of time` (`d` 1 1 2010) `other hearing` `no court: it was a settlement agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the grant's own wording.
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) `other not hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `other grounds` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `settled otherwise` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC hearing` `no court: it was a settlement agreement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `pending` (`d` 1 1 2010) `SC hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The commencement edge.
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 14 6 2017) `SC hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this court set aside my earlier judgment or settlement` `limitation judgment` (`d` 15 6 2017) `SC hearing` `the same court` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 54(5)(b), (c) -- what the court may take into account`

#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `settled out of time` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the damages and the costs`
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `settled out of time` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the damages`
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the costs`
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `LPN judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the costs`
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `nothing: no damages or costs were paid or are payable`
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `nothing: the court does not consider it just and reasonable`
-- Only the court hearing the action: (6) extends only the power to set aside.
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `limitation judgment` (`d` 1 1 2010) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `other grounds` (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `limitation judgment` (`d` 14 6 2017) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the damages and the costs`
#ASSERT `What may the court take into account from my earlier case` `limitation judgment` (`d` 15 6 2017) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
